# chytra-budka USB-flash allowlist — TEMPLATE
#
# Copy to devices.txt and put YOUR boards' MACs in it:
#
#     cp firmware/tools/devices.txt.example firmware/tools/devices.txt
#
# devices.txt itself is gitignored: it is a list of your real hardware, it is
# operator-local, and it should never end up in a public repo via `git add -A`.
#
# Format: one MAC per line, lowercase, no colons — the same 12 hex digits that
# the /dev/esp32-<mac> udev symlink is named after (see host/README.md for the
# udev rule). A '#' comment may follow the MAC after whitespace.
#
# Only MACs listed here can be flashed through tools/flash_safe.sh. Field /
# OTA-only boards must stay OFF this list — that is the entire point of the
# wrapper: production eFuse burns are irreversible, and a distracted
# `idf.py -p /dev/ttyACM0 flash` against the wrong physical board can brick a
# field unit or push an unsigned dev build onto one that must stay signed.
#
# The placeholder lines below are not real boards; replace them.

aabbccddee01  # bench board (USB test rig, freely flashable)
aabbccddee02  # second bench board
